  "raw_ratio_note": "On the UNWEIGHTED club/interaction ratio the extremes are 'window' (24.01) and 'park' (0.19), but both carry weight 0.05/0.05 and are therefore inert in the composite. Judge saturation on the weighted basis.",
  "scale_note": "median_gap is only comparable to the threshold for candidates that keep the fit SCALE (the offset families a and b). The z-scored candidates report a gap in standard-deviation units, so their median_gap flag is not meaningful and only their share/distinct counts should be read.",
  "reading": "score[player][club] splits into a player main effect (irrelevant WITHIN a list), a CLUB main effect (identical on every list, so it is the monopoly) and an INTERACTION (the only term that can hand a different club a different player). 'behavior' is the saturated component: it supplies 63.7% of the composite's club main effect but only 12.2% of its interaction, it is 69.8% club variance against 1.4% interaction, and its top-1 club LAD wins 1.0000 of the class on an average of 1.0 clubs tied. 'need' is the player signal: 75.6% of the composite's interaction and only 17.2% of its club effect. NO weight on a saturated component de-monopolizes; it only sets how loudly the monopoly speaks."
